  "year": 2023,
  "arxivId": "2210.12547",
  "abstract": "SurCo is a framework that learns linear surrogate costs to solve combinatorial nonlinear optimization problems efficiently. It leverages existing combinatorial solvers and can be used in various applications, including embedding table sharding, inverse photonic design, and nonlinear route planning.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "SurCo learns a linear surrogate cost function to solve combinatorial nonlinear optimization problems. This approach combines the flexibility of gradient-based methods with the structure of linear combinatorial optimization, allowing for efficient solutions to complex problems. <strong>Key insight:</strong> by learning a linear surrogate, we can leverage existing efficient combinatorial solvers to find good solutions to nonlinear problems.",
