    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "SurCo works by learning a linear surrogate cost function that can be used in existing combinatorial solvers. The surrogate cost function is learned end-to-end with a nonlinear loss function by differentiating through the linear surrogate solver. This approach allows SurCo to <strong>combine the benefits of gradient-based methods and combinatorial optimization</strong>.",
